    <string name="aimi_iob_surveillance_guard_title">IOB surveillance (anti-stacking)</string>
    <string name="aimi_iob_surveillance_guard_summary">When BG is above target with meaningful IOB, the trend is no longer a fast rise (plateau), and predictions point downward, SMB is capped and temp basal is slightly favoured so onboard insulin can act—without blocking sharp rises or strong meal absorption (COB/UAM). Meal-rise bypass: Δ≥2.0 or short-avg≥2.5 mg/dL/5m while meal-priority context is on. Constants: InsulinStackingStance.kt. Analytics: adjustments.iob_surveillance in Documents/AAPS/AIMI_Decisions.jsonl each loop.</string>
    <string name="aimi_iob_surveillance_applied">IOB surveillance: high active insulin and falling prediction — SMB reduced; prefer TBR. Wait for stacked insulin to work.</string>
